{"name":"Santa Fe Sunset","hex":"#a75a4c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"santa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Santa (noun)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/santa"},{"term":"sunset","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment each evening when the sun disappears below the western horizon.","The changes in color of the sky before and after sunset."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santa Claus","blocks":[{"text":"Santa Claus is a legendary figure originating in Western Christian culture who is said to bring gifts during the late evening and overnight hours on Christmas Eve. Christmas elves are said to make the gifts in Santa's workshop, while flying reindeer pull his sleigh through the air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Merry_Old_Santa_Claus_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg/330px-Merry_Old_Santa_Claus_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Claus"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset"},{"title":"Sunset (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color sunset is a pale tint of orange. It is a representation of the average color of clouds when the sunlight from a sunset is reflected from them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Sunset_2007-1.jpg/330px-Sunset_2007-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/500px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/1280px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/500px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Ghost of Christmas Present as illustrated by John Leech for Charles Dickens's A Christmas Carol (1843)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png/330px-08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png/330px-08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1850 illustration of Saint Nicholas and his servant Père Fouettard/Zwarte Piet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A08_St._Ni